---
scope: src/app/_shared/listSitePages
alignment: unreviewed
description: The one list of every indexable page on the site, each with its canonical URL, title, description, kind, breadcrumb, share image and dates proven by version history.
intent: >
  Every surface that names or dates a page (the sitemap, feed, llms files,
  markdown copies, share cards, visible dates and structured data) reads from
  this one list, so none of them can disagree. It lists every indexable page
  exactly once, each with its canonical URL, title, description, kind,
  breadcrumb trail, share image, markdown copy link where one exists, and the
  first-published and last-modified dates its version history proves. A date it
  cannot prove is left out, never guessed.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - Every indexable page appears exactly once — home, the docs index, every docs section index and doc, /brain and its recipes, /observer, /privacy, the /learn index and each /learn page.
    - Each page carries its canonical URL with a trailing slash, its own title, description, kind, breadcrumb trail and share image, and a markdown copy link exactly when a markdown copy of it exists.
    - A page with one content source carries the first-published and last-modified dates its version history records for that source.
    - Home, /brain, /observer, /privacy, the docs index and the /learn index carry no last-modified date, because no single content source dates them.
    - The sitemap, feed, llms files, markdown copies, share cards, visible dates and structured data all take their pages and dates from this list, so no two of them show a page differently.
  undesired:
    - A build, deploy or checkout date standing in for any page's first-published or last-modified date.
    - A guessed last-modified date on a page that has no single content source.
    - An unindexable page such as the 404 in the list, a page listed twice, or an indexable page left out.
    - A build from a shallow version history that completes with dates that look real but are wrong, instead of failing.
    - A surface that keeps its own page list or works out its own dates, so two surfaces can disagree about what exists or when it changed.
    - A page's breadcrumb, share image or markdown copy link that belongs to another page or points at a copy that does not exist.
---
